course: dictionary
lesson: 10010
title: Temperate: neither too hot nor too cold
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Temperate means mild. A temperate place is never extremely hot or extremely cold. It has warm summers, cool winters and usually four seasons.
explain: «The temperate zones lie between the tropics and the poles and have four seasons.» The tropics are hot and the poles are cold, so temperate zones sit in the middle, away from both extremes. Ask yourself: is this place ever extremely hot or cold? If not, it is probably temperate.
explain: Temperate can also describe a person. A temperate person stays calm and keeps their feelings and habits under control. The clue is the same idea: they do not go to extremes, so they do not explode with anger or sulk for days.
fact: Temperate means never extremely hot or extremely cold.
fact: Earth has three climate zones: tropical (hot), temperate (mild) and polar (very cold).
fact: Temperate zones have four seasons, with warm summers and cool winters.
fact: The UK, Ireland, New Zealand and most of the USA have temperate climates.
fact: Temperate forests lose their leaves in autumn, while temperate rainforests are cool and wet.
exercise: «The temperate zones lie between the tropics and the poles.» Where are the temperate zones? | Only at the North Pole | Deep under the sea | *Between the tropics and the poles | Right on the equator
exercise: What does temperate mean for a place? | Very hot all year round | *Mild, never extremely hot or cold | Very cold all year round | Covered in ice all year
exercise: «Temperate forests lose their leaves in autumn.» What happens to the trees in autumn? | They grow new leaves every day | They turn into ice | They stop growing for ever | *They lose their leaves
test: «Mia stayed temperate, even when the game was lost.» What does temperate mean here? | Very cold and quiet | *Calm and in control of her feelings | Very angry and shouting | Hot and bothered
test: A place with warm summers, cool winters and four seasons has which kind of climate? | Tropical | *Temperate | Polar
exam: Which of these is a temperate place? | *Ireland | The hottest desert in the world | Inside the polar circle | Right on the equator
